From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CatPieLeaf <catpieleaf@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 00:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amd/display: complete cursor vblank events immediately

Intermittent flip_done/commit wait timeouts have been widely reported
on amdgpu since kernel 6.12 (RX 580 through RX 9070 XT), including on
this p03 kernel: 3440x1440@144Hz over DP on an RX 9070 XT (Navi 48)
hits repeated

  [drm] *ERROR* [CRTC:117:crtc-0] flip_done timed out
  [drm] *ERROR* [PLANE:113:plane-7] commit wait timed out

dm_arm_vblank_event() in amdgpu_dm.c defers cursor-only commit events
by stashing them in acrtc->event for amdgpu_dm_crtc_handle_vblank()
(amdgpu_dm_crtc.c) to send on a later vblank:

  } else if (cursor_update) {
          acrtc->event = acrtc->base.state->event;
          acrtc->base.state->event = NULL;
  }

That handler's send condition is:

  if (acrtc->event && acrtc->pflip_status != AMDGPU_FLIP_SUBMITTED)

which is also true for the idle AMDGPU_FLIP_NONE state, not just a
genuinely pending cursor event. If a real page flip is armed on this
CRTC before the deferred cursor event is ever picked up, dm_arm_vblank_event()'s
pflip_update branch overwrites the same acrtc->event field (its own
WARN_ON(acrtc->event) firing is the tell), and the cursor event's
matching drm_crtc_vblank_get() reference is never balanced by a put.
Either the wrong event ships or one is dropped, leaving DC waiting on
a flip completion that already got consumed out of order - manifesting
as the flip_done/commit wait timeouts above.

This got much easier to hit after commit 58a261bfc967 ("drm/amd/display:
use a more lax vblank enable policy for older ASICs") shortened the
vblank off-delay, making vblank enable/disable toggle far more often
between commits and widening how often this race window gets exercised.
Tracked upstream at:
https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/drm/amd/-/issues/3787

Fix it the same way genuine page-flip and pageflip-IRQ completions
already do elsewhere in this file (dm_pflip_high_irq(),
amdgpu_dm_crtc_handle_vblank() itself): since a cursor update is
already committed to hardware by the time we get here, there's no
reason to defer its event at all. Send it immediately and balance the
vblank reference dm_arm_vblank_event_pre_programming() took for it,
instead of leaving it for the generic vblank handler to race against.

Backport of an unmerged amd-gfx fix by Michele Palazzi
("drm/amd/display: complete cursor vblank events immediately",
amd-gfx, 2026-02-17), adapted to this kernel's current
dm_arm_vblank_event() layout.

Signed-off-by: CatPieLeaf <catpieleaf@proton.me>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c | 16 +++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c
@@ -10271,8 +10271,20 @@ static void dm_arm_vblank_event(struct amdgpu_crtc *acrtc,
 			      "crtc:%d, pflip_stat:AMDGPU_FLIP_SUBMITTED\n",
 			      acrtc->crtc_id);
 	} else if (cursor_update) {
-		acrtc->event = acrtc->base.state->event;
-		acrtc->base.state->event = NULL;
+		/*
+		 * Cursor updates are committed to hardware immediately, so
+		 * complete the event now instead of deferring it into
+		 * acrtc->event for amdgpu_dm_crtc_handle_vblank() to send on
+		 * a later vblank. Deferring it left a window where a
+		 * subsequent real page flip's arm above could clobber this
+		 * stashed cursor event before it was ever sent, and where
+		 * that handler's "pflip_status != AMDGPU_FLIP_SUBMITTED"
+		 * check (also true for the idle AMDGPU_FLIP_NONE state)
+		 * could send or drop the wrong flip's event under load.
+		 */
+		drm_crtc_send_vblank_event(&acrtc->base, acrtc->base.state->event);
+		acrtc->base.state->event = NULL;
+		drm_crtc_vblank_put(&acrtc->base);
 	}
 }
 
